---
/**
 * K Culture Wire — 사다리 꼭대기가 얼마나 자리를 지키나. (/ladder-churn)
 *
 * ── 왜 이 지면인가 ─────────────────────────────────────────────
 * 우리는 이 수집에서 `veteran`(오래 머문 사람)과 `hot_streak`(연승 중인 사람)을
 * **한 번도 쓴 적이 없다.** `/esports` 도 `/ladder-gap` 도 안 쓴다.
 * 승률·LP 는 「얼마나 센가」이고, 이 둘은 **「얼마나 자주 바뀌나」**다. 다른 질문이다.
 *
 * ── 우리 esports 지면 셋이 세 가지 자로 같은 말을 한다 ─────────
 *   `/esports`     한국 챌린저 승률이 여섯 중 꼴찌 — 상대가 세다
 *   `/ladder-gap`  한국은 위층과 아래층 차가 가장 작다 — 저변이 두껍다
 *   여기          한국 꼭대기가 가장 안 바뀐다 — 그 두꺼움이 자리를 굳혔다
 * 자가 다른데 결론이 같으면 그건 우연이 아니다. **다만 인과로는 안 쓴다.**
 *
 * ── ⚠ 나흘이다 ────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * 8/5 는 키 만료로 비었고 소급이 안 된다. 결측을 지면에 적는다.
 * 「추세」가 아니라 **순서가 안 바뀐다**는 확인이다.
 *
 * ⛔ 일본은 챌린저 50명이라 다른 곳의 6분의 1이다. 싣되 기대지 않는다.
 * ⛔ 광고 자리를 만들지 않았다. Riot Production 승인 전이다.
 */
import WikiTip from '../../layouts/WikiTip.astro';
import KcwRelatedArticles from '../../components/KcwRelatedArticles.astro';
import data from '../../data/wikitip-ladder-churn.json';

const TITLE = 'Who stays at the top of the ladder';
const DESC =
  'Korea has the most settled top tier of six League of Legends regions — 54% of its challengers are '
  + 'long-standing, against 36.8% in North America, which has the most players on hot streaks.';

const kr = data.rows.find((r) => r.code === 'kr')!;
const na = data.rows.find((r) => r.code === 'na1')!;

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Dataset',
  name: TITLE,
  description: DESC,
  temporalCoverage: data.day,
  creator: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'K Culture Wire' },
  isBasedOn: ['https://developer.riotgames.com'],
};
---

<WikiTip title={TITLE} description={DESC} jsonLd={jsonLd} canonical="https://www.kculturewire.com/ladder-churn">
  <h1>Who stays at the top of the ladder</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Win rate says how hard a tier is. It does not say how often the people in it change.
    Riot marks two things we have never used: which players are long-standing in their tier, and
    which are on a winning streak. Collected {data.day} at {data.collectedAt.slice(11, 16)} KST.
  </p>
  {/* ⭐ 2026-08-22 — 날짜는 적혀 있었는데 「그날 수다」라는 말이 없었다. 날짜만 있으면 손님은
      오늘 수로 읽는다. 자(check-kcw-stale-stamp)가 이 칸을 지킨다 */}
  <p class="note">
    <strong>That is the day it was measured, and we are not collecting at the moment.</strong> Our
    developer key expires every 24 hours and production approval is still pending, so this is one
    dated day rather than a running series. A ladder cannot be measured backwards, so the days since
    are gone rather than pending.
  </p>

  <section>
    <h2>Korea’s top is the most settled. North America’s turns over hardest.</h2>
    <div class="flip">
      <div>
        <span class="lab">Korea — long-standing challengers</span>
        <span class="big">{kr.vetPc}%</span>
        <span class="det">
          {kr.veteran} of {kr.players}. The highest of the six, on every day measured.
          {kr.hotPc}% are on a hot streak.
        </span>
      </div>
      <div>
        <span class="lab">North America — the mirror</span>
        <span class="big">{na.vetPc}%</span>
        <span class="det">
          {na.veteran} of {na.players} long-standing, the lowest — while <b>{na.hotPc}%</b> are on a
          hot streak, the highest. Fewer settled players, more players surging.
        </span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>All six, most settled first</h2>
    <div class="scroll-x">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Region</th><th>Challengers</th><th>Long-standing</th><th>Share</th>
            <th>On a hot streak</th><th>Share</th><th>Grandmaster long-standing</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {data.rows.map((r) => (
            <tr class={r.code === 'kr' ? 'me' : ''}>
              <td class="nm">{r.region}</td>
              <td>{r.players}</td>
              <td>{r.veteran}</td><td class="tot">{r.vetPc}%</td>
              <td>{r.hot}</td><td>{r.hotPc}%</td>
              <td>{r.gmVetPc}%</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="note">
      The two columns move against each other. Where fewer players are settled, more are climbing —
      which is what churn looks like when you only get to see one night of it. Korea sits at one end
      of both, North America at the other, and the four regions between them line up in the same order
      on each measure.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Long-standing share, every day we have measured</h2>
    <p class="sub">Percent of challengers. {data.days} days — a check that the ordering holds, not a trend.</p>
    <div class="scroll-x">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Date</th>{data.regions.map((r) => <th>{r}</th>)}</tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {data.series.map((s) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="nm">{s.date}</td>
              {data.regions.map((r) => (
                <td class={r === 'Korea' ? 'tot' : ''}>
                  {(s as Record<string, number | string>)[r] ?? '—'}
                </td>
              ))}
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="note">
      Korea is highest on all {data.days} days and North America lowest on all {data.days}.{' '}
      <b>2026-08-05 is missing</b> — the collection key expired, and a ladder cannot be rebuilt
      afterwards, so the day is gone rather than filled in.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Three measures, one direction</h2>
    <p class="sub">This is the third thing we have counted about the same six ladders. They do not disagree.</p>
    <ul class="three">
      <li><b><a href="/esports">Win rate</a></b> — Korea’s challengers win least often of the six. Their opponents are the hardest.</li>
      <li><b><a href="/ladder-gap">Tier gap</a></b> — Korea’s top 300 beat the 700 below them by the smallest margin. The field beneath is closest.</li>
      <li><b>Turnover</b> — Korea’s top tier changes hands least. That field has settled into it.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="note">
      Three different fields of the same nightly call, pointing the same way. That is worth stating
      and worth not over-stating: these are three views of one population, not three independent
      confirmations, and none of them explains <i>why</i>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <KcwRelatedArticles page="/ladder-churn" />

  <section class="src">
    <h2>Where these numbers come from</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Riot Games</b> — Developer API, {data.endpoints}. Collected once a day at 22:00 KST.</li>
      <li>
        <b>“Long-standing” and “hot streak” are Riot’s own flags</b>, returned per player on the
        league entry. We count how many carry each flag and divide by the tier size; we do not define
        either term ourselves and cannot see the threshold behind them.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Japan is a sixth the size</b> — {data.rows.find((r) => r.code === 'jp1')!.players} challengers
        against roughly 300 elsewhere. Its percentages move by two points for one player, and are
        printed without being leaned on.
      </li>
      <li><b>{data.privacy}</b></li>
      <li>
        <b>Four days is a snapshot.</b> Nothing here says turnover is rising or falling anywhere. What
        it says is that the six regions sat in the same order on each of the days we looked.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <p class="back"><a href="/">&larr; Back to the front page</a></p>
</WikiTip>

<style>
  h1 { margin: 0 0 .5rem; font-size: 1.7rem; letter-spacing: -.02em; }
  .lead { margin: 0 0 2rem; font-size: 1rem; color: var(--muted); }
  section { margin: 0 0 2.5rem; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.1rem; margin: 0 0 .6rem; letter-spacing: -.01em; line-height: 1.4; }
  .sub { font-size: .87rem; color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 1rem; line-height: 1.6; }
  .note { font-size: .82rem; color: var(--muted); margin: .9rem 0 0; line-height: 1.6; }

  .flip { display: grid; gap: .8rem; grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  @media (min-width: 34rem) { .flip { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } }
  .flip > div { background: var(--card); border-radius: 8px; padding: .9rem 1rem; }
  .lab { display: block; font-size: .76rem; letter-spacing: .04em; text-transform: uppercase;
         color: var(--muted); font-weight: 700; }
  .big { display: block; font-size: 1.6rem; font-weight: 700; margin: .25rem 0 .35rem;
         letter-spacing: -.01em; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .det { display: block; font-size: .78rem; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.55; }

  .three { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.1rem; font-size: .88rem; line-height: 1.7; }
  .three li { margin: .4rem 0; }

  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: .84rem; }
  th, td { padding: .45rem .55rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); text-align: right;
           white-space: nowrap; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  th { font-size: .71rem; letter-spacing: .03em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted);
       font-weight: 700; }
  th:first-child, td.nm { text-align: left; }
  td.tot { font-weight: 700; }
  tr.me td { background: var(--card); }

  .src ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.1rem; font-size: .85rem; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.7; }
  .src li { margin: .45rem 0; }
  .src b { color: var(--ink); }
  .back { margin-top: 2.5rem; font-size: .9rem; }
</style>
